<title>USA: Time Warner holders approve Turner deal.</title>
<headline>Time Warner holders approve Turner deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner Inc shareholders overwhelmingly approved the merger with Turner Broadcasting System Inc, creating the world's largest entertainment group, Time Warner Chairman Gerald Levin said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Levin gave no preliminary vote totals at the end of a special Time Warner shareholders meeting in New York, but said the transaction bringing together some of the best known names in entertainment and news should close at 1800 ET Thursday if Turner shareholders approve the deal at a separate meeting set for 1400 ET.</p>
<p>-- Michael Connor 212-859-1713</p>
</text>
